            <div xml:id="d1242">

                <pb facs="1099" n="785" xml:id="pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72115/308</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) to the Secretary of State </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-12-08">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 8, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11:45 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>1222. Bryce suggests I transmit following telegram which he has received from
                    bliss, president American Syrian College at Beirut:</p>
                <p>British non-combatants including women ordered to interior as hostages pending
                    release of detained Ottomans. Shall deeply appreciate any measures to avert this
                    action made sinister by holy war proclamation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
